# Both Dockerfiles COPY . . from the repo root and then run their own
# pnpm install/build steps -- without this file, that COPY picks up
# whatever node_modules/dist/.next a local `docker build` invocation's host
# happens to have on disk, silently masking a Dockerfile step that doesn't
# actually (re)build something it depends on. Found for real, not
# hypothetical: TASK-040's own local `docker build -f apps/web/Dockerfile`
# "verified" successfully only because host-local packages/sdk/dist/ leaked
# into the build context, while the Dockerfile itself never built @lis/sdk
# -- CI's clean checkout (no such leftover dist/) caught the real gap this
# local build couldn't. Mirrors .gitignore's own exclusions.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.next
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/storybook-static
.env
.env.local
**/*.log
.git
